      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide\n\n## Introduction\nWelcome to the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide. This document provides essential information for setting up and using the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor in an industrial environment.\n\n## Specifications\n- **Component**: Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor (Industrial Grade)\n- **Voltage**: 12V-24V DC\n- **Interface**: I2C\n- **Setup**: Mount to bracket, connect wiring harness to terminal block, ensure no debris on lens, power on, run 'N7_INIT' diagnostic via console.\n- **Safety**: Do not expose to liquids; ensure grounding is complete before power-up; avoid direct laser light on lens.\n- **Troubleshooting**: If LED flashes red, check voltage; if no response, check I2C address settings.\n\n## Setup Instructions\n1. Mount the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor to the provided bracket.\n2. Connect the wiring harness to the terminal block, ensuring all connections are secure.\n3. Clean the sensor lens to remove any debris.\n4. Power on the sensor and run the 'N7_INIT' diagnostic via the console to verify proper operation.\n\n## Safety",
